---
/* THE INTRODUCTION, IN THE ORIGINAL'S SHAPE.

   "designing products & / human experience." was the line here, and its
   proportions were right: a long first line resolving onto a short second, set
   large enough that the mark overlaps it. That is the composition — the type
   and the object share the same space rather than taking turns — and it is
   restored exactly. Only two things about it changed.

   THE WORDS NAME THE PERSON. The old line could have sat on any studio's
   homepage; a portfolio's first line has one job the work itself cannot do.
   The second line is kept whole, so the sentence still lands where it always
   landed and only the opening is new.

   THE FILL IS SOLID. The halftone was the site's signature while the headline
   was a mood line you took in as a shape — but the grid is a fixed 3.5px
   whatever the type does, so a stem always resolved to a dashed outline of
   itself. That is a texture, and a name has to be read. Same family, same
   weight, same tracking, same size; only the ink is continuous now.

   Each line is its own block and never wraps — the break is the design. .ln-i
   is what the arrival translates behind .ln's clip. */
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="d1 dotted"><span class="ln"><span class="ln-i">i&rsquo;m himalay, designing</span></span><span class="ln"><span class="ln-i">human experience.</span></span></h1>
  </div>

  <div class="stage">
    <!-- live raymarched glass hash. no shadow, no backdrop. -->
    <canvas id="hashgl" aria-label="Glass hash symbol"></canvas>
    <img class="hash-fallback" src="/assets/img/hash-clean.png" alt="Glass hash symbol" width="660" height="820" />
  </div>
</section>
